## 3. Splunk Connectivity (the one piece awesome-copilot doesn't provide)

Use a Splunk MCP server so agents can run SPL directly:

1. **Official Splunk MCP Server** — [Splunkbase app 7931](https://splunkbase.splunk.com/app/7931), runs inside Splunk (Cloud or Enterprise 9.4+), exposes search over MCP.
2. **[splunk/splunk-mcp-server2](https://github.com/splunk/splunk-mcp-server2)** — standalone Python/TypeScript server; runs searches, returns JSON/CSV/Markdown, and ships **input SPL validation guardrails and output sanitization** — valuable given Shareworks logs may contain participant PII.

Recommended setup:

- Dedicated **read-only** Splunk service account/token, scoped to only the Shareworks app indexes
- Enforce a search-window cap (e.g., max 7 days) and result cap in the MCP server config
- Output sanitization ON: strip/emails, SSN-like patterns, account numbers before they reach the model
- Register in the repo's MCP config so it works in VS Code and Copilot CLI; add via repo settings for the Copilot coding agent later

