## 6. Phased Rollout

**Phase 0 — Foundations (week 1–2)**
Stand up Splunk MCP server (read-only token, sanitization on). Run `acquire-codebase-knowledge` on the monolith to generate `docs/codebase/`. Add Java + code-review instruction files to the repo. Validate the MCP connection from VS Code.

**Phase 1 — On-demand triage (week 3–4)**
Build `sw-splunk-triage` + `sw-spl-playbook` + `sw-defect-dossier`. Pilot with the on-call rotation; tune signature normalization and noise exclusions. Success metric: dossier quality (does on-call trust it?), time-to-identify.

**Phase 2 — RCA + fix drafting (week 5–8)**
Build `sw-root-cause` and `sw-fix-engineer` with the review gate. Measure RCA accuracy against engineer-confirmed root causes; track % of drafted fixes accepted with minor/no edits. Package everything as the `shareworks-defect-hunter` plugin for one-command install across the team.

**Phase 3 — Automation (week 9+)**
- **Scheduled scan:** GitHub Actions workflow (pattern: awesome-copilot `workflows/`) runs the triage agent hourly/daily via Copilot CLI in headless mode; new dossiers become enriched GitHub/Jira issues.
- **Alert-driven:** Splunk saved-search alert → webhook → `repository_dispatch` → assign the issue to the **Copilot coding agent**, which runs RCA + fix and opens a draft PR (human still merges).
- Add `tool-guardian` + `audit-logger` hooks before enabling any scheduled runs.

**Phase 4 — Hardening & metrics**
Dashboard: defects auto-triaged, mean-time-to-RCA, fix acceptance rate, false-positive rate. Feed misses back into the SPL playbook and stacktrace-mapping rules — the skills are living documents.

