## 7. Risks & Guardrails (stock-plan platform specifics)

- **PII/financial data in logs** — sanitize at the MCP layer, never in the prompt; forbid raw log excerpts in PR descriptions and Jira tickets (dossier template enforces this)
- **Read-only telemetry** — the Splunk token can search only; agents never write to Splunk
- **Change control / SOX** — human approval gate is structural (separate agent hand-off), not just a prompt instruction; audit-logger hook records every session
- **Monolith scale** — RCA quality depends on Phase 0's codebase docs; refresh them on a schedule (a `workflows/` cron job can do this)
- **Hallucinated root causes** — RCA report must cite an evidence chain (event → line → commit) and confidence level; `critical-thinking`/`devils-advocate` persona rules force alternatives to be listed
- **Cost control** — time-boxed investigation phases (from `aws-incident-triage`) and search-window caps stop runaway agent loops

